  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Serum Magnesium Level</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Below Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Hypomagnesemia (low magnesium levels) may be indicative of magnesium deficiency, malabsorption disorders, kidney disease, certain medications, or hormonal imbalances. Further evaluation is needed to determine the underlying cause and appropriate treatment.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Serum magnesium levels within the normal range indicate an adequate magnesium status.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Above Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Hypermagnesemia (high magnesium levels) can occur in conditions such as kidney dysfunction, excessive magnesium supplementation, or adrenal insufficiency. Clinical correlation is necessary to determine the underlying cause and management approach.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
